    "https://eou.peopleadmin.com/postings/1951": {
      "title": "University Jobs",
      "description": "University Jobs at EOU | Outdoor Activities--Adjunct Pool in Health and Human Performance Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help EOU Home HR Home HR Contacts About Union County Outdoor Activities--Adjunct Pool in Health and Human Performance Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must provide:\r\n1.\tLetter of application (which should include why this position is attractive to the applicant, how it meets the applicant’s professional goals, and what attracts the applicant to EOU’s Outdoor Activities program).\r\n2.\tResume/Curriculum vitae with the names, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three professional references.\r\n3.\t1-page Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (KSA’s) addendum listing experience and qualifications. (Submit under Portfolio 1)\r\n4.\tCopies of current certifications. (Submit under Portfolio 2) Posting Details Position Information Position Number Position Title Outdoor Activities--Adjunct Pool in Health and Human Performance Job Description Summary EOU is soliciting adjunct applications for qualified instructors in the following academic discipline: The College of Science, Technology, Mathematics, and Health Sciences at Eastern Oregon University is recruiting to establish an adjunct instructor applicant pool to teach outdoor activity ( OUT ) courses in Physical Activity and Health and Human Performance. The appointment begins based on departmental needs but no earlier than September 16, 2021. See webpage for full OUT course offerings: https://www.eou.edu/outdoor/out-courses/ Responsibilities Teaching responsibilities would include 1, 2, or 3-credit classes in outdoor activities focused on introductory or intermediate level skill sets. Particular course offerings may vary depending on department needs and adjunct instructor qualifications. *Creates an environment that acknowledges, encourages and celebrates differences. *Functions and communicates effectively and respectfully within the context of varying beliefs, behaviors, orientations, identities and cultural backgrounds. *Seeks opportunities to gain experience working and collaborating in diverse, multicultural, and inclusive settings with a willingness to change for continual improvement. *Adheres to all EOU’s policies including the policies on Prohibited Discrimination & Harassment and the Professional Standards of Conduct. Required Qualifications •\tA high school diploma or GED . •\tCommitment to excellence in teaching at the undergraduate level. •\tCurrent certification in CPR /First-Aid •\t2-year minimum experience directly related to topic/course to be instructing. •\tValid driver’s license. *Documented capability to learn online learning software application(s) *Ability to effectively inspire and teach students from diverse backgrounds and learning styles in online education environment *Successful completion of a EOU background check and submission of valid work authorization documents Preferred Qualifications •\tAn undergraduate degree or Master’s Degree from an accredited institution in a related field to the course offering. •\t2-year experience in leadership and/or instructing position. •\tCurrent certification in Wilderness First Aid ( WFA ) or Wilderness First Responder ( WFR ) or Emergency Medical Technician ( EMT ). Candidate demonstrated at least one year of instructing in the topic being taught •\tExperience guiding groups of youth or adults in semi-remote natural settings. •\tAny certifications specific to the related field. *Competency in the use of an online learning management software application(s) ( i.e. CANVAS , Blackboard, etc.) Posting Detail Information Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Summary Applicants must provide: 1.\tLetter of application (which should include why this position is attractive to the applicant, how it meets the applicant’s professional goals, and what attracts the applicant to EOU’s Outdoor Activities program). 2.\tResume/Curriculum vitae with the names, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three professional references. 3.\t1-page Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (KSA’s) addendum listing experience and qualifications. (Submit under Portfolio 1) 4.\tCopies of current certifications. (Submit under Portfolio 2) Quick Link to Posting https://eou.peopleadmin.com/postings/1376 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? EOU Website Posting Chronicle of Higher Education State Employment Service DiverseJobs.net Referral by EOU Employee HigherEdJobs.com Newspaper Other If you answered \"Newspaper\" or \"Other\" above, please give specifics here: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Portfolio (document1) Portfolio (document2) Optional Documents Transcripts Statement of Teaching Philosophy To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
