    "https://eou.peopleadmin.com/postings/3504": {
      "title": "University Jobs",
      "description": "University Jobs at EOU | Clinical Mental Health Counseling Part-Time Online Educator/Adjunct Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help EOU Home HR Home HR Contacts About Union County Clinical Mental Health Counseling Part-Time Online Educator/Adjunct Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must provide: 1. A letter of application which should include why this position is attractive to the applicant, how it meets the applicant’s professional goals, what attracts the applicant to EOU’s online CMHC program, and specific qualifications for the available open course. (NOTE: For information on what courses are available for upcoming terms, please email CMHC@eou.edu .) 2. Curriculum vitae which includes the names, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three professional references 3. Transcripts (official required for finalists) 4. A one-page statement of teaching philosophy which includes approach to online synchronous and asynchronous teaching 5. A sample syllabus (use “Portfolio 1” in the online application system to upload the syllabus) Only complete files of qualified applicants will be reviewed. Candidates are encouraged to review the values and principles of Eastern Oregon University . Eastern Oregon University is an EEO Employer and welcomes applications from women, members of historically underrepresented minority groups, US Veterans, and persons with disabilities. Posting Details Position Information Position Number Position Title Clinical Mental Health Counseling Part-Time Online Educator/Adjunct Job Description Summary The Clinical Mental Health Counseling program in the College of Science, Technology, Mathematics, and Health Sciences at Eastern Oregon University ( EOU ) is recruiting for part-time online educator/adjunct instructor(s) to teach courses in the Clinical Mental Health Counseling Program. EOU’s Clinical Mental Health Counseling program is a fully online program. EOU is interested in applicants who are committed to assisting our students in reaching their professional goals. Appointments are on an as-needed basis and would begin as early as Spring Term 2024. Courses may include but are not limited to: Counseling and Helping Relationships, Diagnostic Systems and Psychopathology, Group Counseling, Counseling Substance Use Disorders, and other core curriculum courses. Course availability will change from term to term. See webpage for full program information: https://www.eou.edu/clinical-mental-health-counseling/ Responsibilities Part-time online educators/adjuncts will be responsible for: Teaching and engaging with graduate students in the CMHC program Running and building/adding to curated online courses Being available to meet for synchronous courses in the evening (Pacific Time), and on weekends for Residency courses Being committed to ensuring that every student is a full member of the EOU community and that all community members recognize, promote and take advantage of the educational and cultural value of diversity. Demonstrating the ability to work collaboratively with other educators and staff and collaborate to identify and solve problems and engage in program improvement Required Qualifications Ph.D. degree from a CACREP accredited institution in Counselor Education and Supervision · Two or more years of relevant experience in counseling, counselor education, and/or supervision Higher education, online teaching experience Minimum of one year of direct counseling experience Must satisfactorily complete EOU criminal and credential background check Valid work authorization documents are required . In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. Eastern Oregon University does not sponsor applicants for employment visas. Preferred Qualifications Licensed Mental Health Counselor ( LMHC ), Licensed Professional Counselor ( LPC ), or eligible for licensure in state of residence Experience supervising master’s level clinical mental health counseling students Credentialed or ability to be credentialed as a clinical supervisor (e.g., Approved Clinical Supervisor ( ACS ) and/or a state level supervisory status) Experience utilizing the LMS Canvas Experience designing, developing, and teaching curated, online courses Working knowledge of CACREP Standards Posting Detail Information Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Summary Applicants must provide: 1. A letter of application which should include why this position is attractive to the applicant, how it meets the applicant’s professional goals, what attracts the applicant to EOU’s online CMHC program, and specific qualifications for the available open course. ( NOTE : For information on what courses are available for upcoming terms, please email CMHC@eou.edu .) 2. Curriculum vitae which includes the names, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three professional references 3. Transcripts (official required for finalists) 4. A one-page statement of teaching philosophy which includes approach to online synchronous and asynchronous teaching 5. A sample syllabus (use “Portfolio 1” in the online application system to upload the syllabus) Only complete files of qualified applicants will be reviewed. Candidates are encouraged to review the values and principles of Eastern Oregon University . Eastern Oregon University is an EEO Employer and welcomes applications from women, members of historically underrepresented minority groups, US Veterans, and persons with disabilities. Quick Link to Posting https://eou.peopleadmin.com/postings/2950 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? EOU Website Posting Chronicle of Higher Education State Employment Service DiverseJobs.net Referral by EOU Employee HigherEdJobs.com Newspaper Other If you answered \"Newspaper\" or \"Other\" above, please give specifics here: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Transcripts Portfolio (document1) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://eou.peopleadmin.com/postings/3601": {
      "title": "University Jobs at EOU | Academic Advisor/Healthcare Programs Coordinator",
      "description": "University Jobs at EOU | Academic Advisor/Healthcare Programs Coordinator Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help EOU Home HR Home HR Contacts About Union County Academic Advisor/Healthcare Programs Coordinator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Eastern Oregon University – Oregon’s Rural University! – is a respected public, higher education institution of academic excellence. Outstanding faculty and staff thrive and together fulfill their career ambitions to serve students from all walks of life. Applicant must provide: 1) Letter of application (which should include why this position is attractive to the applicant, how it meets the applicant’s professional goals, and what attracts the applicant to EOU); 2) Resume/Curriculum vitae; 3) Submit names, emails, and phone numbers for at least three references in the reference section of the application. Candidates are encouraged to review the values and principles of Eastern Oregon University . Only complete files of qualified applicants will be reviewed. EOU is a beautiful, quaint campus nestled in the remarkably scenic, high elevation Grande Ronde Valley populated by wonderful, community-minded citizens that have balanced work-life flexibility. Take a virtual tour of Eastern Oregon University . EOU offers a very attractive package of State of Oregon public employee benefits including: • Paid holidays (10 days/year) • Paid vacation (accrues 15 hours/month) • Paid sick time-off (accrues 8 hours/month – no limit!) • Individual AND Family Healthcare Insurance: medical, dental and vision! (95%+ employer-paid!) • Generous Oregon Public Employee Retirement System benefits • Employer paid life insurance • Relocation assistance • Discounted tuition benefits for employees and eligible dependents • Discounted athletics facilities membership • For more details, see Prospective Employees . Eastern Oregon University is an EEO Employer and welcomes applications from women, members of historically underrepresented minority groups, US Veterans, and persons with disabilities. EOU is committed to providing equal opportunity in its recruitment, admissions, educational programs, activities and employment without illegal discrimination on the basis of age, color, disability, national origin, race, marital status, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression or any status as protected by state or federal law. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Academic Advisor/Healthcare Programs Coordinator Full or Part Time Full Time FTE 1.0 Position Type Regular Posting Number 20110706C&A Position Summary Information Job Description Summary Eastern Oregon University ( EOU ) seeks nominations, applications, and expressions of interest for the position of Healthcare Programs Coordinator. The position is a full-time, 12-month, shared position and reports directly to the Executive Director of Enrollment Management. The Academic Advisor/Healthcare Programs Coordinator provides comprehensive academic advising that supports student success, retention, and timely degree completion for both on-campus and online students. The position serves assigned academic disciplines, with primary responsibility for advising students in Science, Technology, Mathematics, and Health Sciences ( STMHS ) programs, including pre-professional healthcare pathways. The incumbent serves as a liaison between Eastern Oregon University and graduate health professional programs, coordinates pre-professional healthcare initiatives, develops advising resources and student opportunities, and collaborates with faculty, staff, and community partners to enhance student success and enrollment goals. Responsibilities Provide comprehensive academic advising for an assigned caseload of on-campus and online students, including first-time, transfer, and continuing students. Guide students regarding degree requirements, academic policies, educational opportunities, career planning, academic progress, and available campus resources. Monitor student progress toward degree completion and implement interventions, referrals, and support strategies to improve student success, retention, and graduation outcomes. Coordinate with faculty advising mentors, university departments, and student support services to address student needs and academic concerns. Develop and implement advising procedures, conduct workshops, trainings, orientation, and outreach activities, and assist students through registration and re-enrollment processes. Maintain accurate advising records and student plans using university information systems, prepare reports, and serve as a subject matter expert for assigned academic programs. Coordinate advising for pre-professional healthcare programs by developing academic plans, communicating application requirements and timelines, maintaining advising materials and program websites, and serving as a liaison with graduate health professional programs. Develop and maintain community partnerships that provide volunteer and job shadowing opportunities, coordinate the EOU Health Speaker Series, advise the Pre-Professional Health Club, and support recruitment, retention, accreditation, and program assessment activities. Minimum Qualifications Education Bachelor’s Degree in a related field Experience Two (2) years working with students in higher education, adult education, student services or student personnel, counseling or social work, or educational administration Two (2) years demonstrating the following required skills: problem-solving and critical thinking; strong written, verbal, and interpersonal ability; research and team skills; organizational and presentation skills; multi-tasking ability; and ability to prioritize work in alignment with the position’s focus Must satisfactorily complete EOU criminal and credential background check. Having a criminal history is not an automatic bar to employment. In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. Eastern Oregon University does not sponsor applicants for employment visas. Preferred Qualifications Education Masters degree in Adult Education, Student Services, Counseling, Educational Administration, or a related field Bilingual or multilingual skills Experience One (1) year of prior academic advising experience with student populations similar to EOU Special Instructions to Applicants Eastern Oregon University – Oregon’s Rural University! – is a respected public, higher education institution of academic excellence. Outstanding faculty and staff thrive and together fulfill their career ambitions to serve students from all walks of life. Applicant must provide: 1) Letter of application (which should include why this position is attractive to the applicant, how it meets the applicant’s professional goals, and what attracts the applicant to EOU ); 2) Resume/Curriculum vitae; 3) Submit names, emails, and phone numbers for at least three references in the reference section of the application. Candidates are encouraged to review the values and principles of Eastern Oregon University . Only complete files of qualified applicants will be reviewed. EOU is a beautiful, quaint campus nestled in the remarkably scenic, high elevation Grande Ronde Valley populated by wonderful, community-minded citizens that have balanced work-life flexibility. Take a virtual tour of Eastern Oregon University . EOU offers a very attractive package of State of Oregon public employee benefits including: • Paid holidays (10 days/year) • Paid vacation (accrues 15 hours/month) • Paid sick time-off (accrues 8 hours/month – no limit!) • Individual AND Family Healthcare Insurance: medical, dental and vision! (95%+ employer-paid!) • Generous Oregon Public Employee Retirement System benefits • Employer paid life insurance • Relocation assistance • Discounted tuition benefits for employees and eligible dependents • Discounted athletics facilities membership • For more details, see Prospective Employees . Eastern Oregon University is an EEO Employer and welcomes applications from women, members of historically underrepresented minority groups, US Veterans, and persons with disabilities. EOU is committed to providing equal opportunity in its recruitment, admissions, educational programs, activities and employment without illegal discrimination on the basis of age, color, disability, national origin, race, marital status, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression or any status as protected by state or federal law. Salary $48,906 to $61,300 Annually DOE Posting Detail Information Open Date 08/19/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes First Day of Application Review 09/02/2026 Quick Link to Posting https://eou.peopleadmin.com/postings/3589 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? EOU Website Posting Chronicle of Higher Education State Employment Service DiverseJobs.net Referral by EOU Employee HigherEdJobs.com Newspaper Other If you answered \"Newspaper\" or \"Other\" above, please give specifics here: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Veteran Preference Document To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
