    "https://eou.peopleadmin.com/postings/3506": {
      "title": "University Jobs at EOU | Psychology Adjunct Instructor Pool",
      "description": "University Jobs at EOU | Psychology Adjunct Instructor Pool Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help EOU Home HR Home HR Contacts About Union County Psychology Adjunct Instructor Pool Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicant must provide: 1) Letter of application (which should include why this position is attractive to the applicant, how it meets the applicant’s professional goals, and what attracts the applicant to EOU’s online program); 2) Curriculum vitae with the names, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three professional references; 3) Transcripts (official will only be required for finalists); 4) One-page statement of teaching philosophy. 5) Sample syllabus (use “Portfolio 1” in the online application system to upload the syllabus) 6) Sample of Learning Management System used for online courses (use “Portfolio 2” in the online application system to upload this documentation). Candidates are encouraged to review the values and principles of Eastern Oregon University . Only complete files of qualified applicants will be reviewed. Eastern Oregon University is an EEO Employer and welcomes applications from women, members of historically underrepresented minority groups, US Veterans, and persons with disabilities. EOU is committed to providing equal opportunity in its recruitment, admissions, educational programs, activities and employment without illegal discrimination on the basis of age, color, disability, national origin, race, marital status, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression or any status as protected by state or federal law. Posting Details Position Information Position Number Position Title Psychology Adjunct Instructor Pool Job Description Summary TThe College of Science, Technology, Mathematics and Health Sciences at Eastern Oregon University is recruiting for an online adjunct instructor pool to teach courses inthe area of clinical psychology . We are specifically looking for instructors qualified to teach undergraduate courses in Psychopathology, Clinical Interventions, and other clinical areas The appointment begins based on departmental need but no earlier than September 16, 2024 . See webpage for full program information: https://www.eou.edu/psych/ Responsibilities he position requires a Ph.D in the area of clinical psychology and previous online teaching experience. The position ensures that every student is a full member of the EOU community and that all community members recognize, promote and take advantage of the educational and cultural value of diversity. Required Qualifications • A Doctorate Degree in clinical psychology from an accredited institution at the time the appointment begins. Candidates nearing completion of their doctorate ( ABD ) will be considered. • Commitment to excellence in teaching at the undergraduate level. • Documented evidence of online teaching experience in higher education • Valid work authorization documents are required. • Must satisfactorily complete EOU criminal and credential background check. Preferred Qualifications • Online teaching experience in Canvas • Online teaching certification Posting Detail Information Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Summary Applicant must provide: 1) Letter of application (which should include why this position is attractive to the applicant, how it meets the applicant’s professional goals, and what attracts the applicant to EOU’s online program); 2) Curriculum vitae with the names, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three professional references; 3) Transcripts (official will only be required for finalists); 4) One-page statement of teaching philosophy. 5) Sample syllabus (use “Portfolio 1” in the online application system to upload the syllabus) 6) Sample of Learning Management System used for online courses (use “Portfolio 2” in the online application system to upload this documentation). Candidates are encouraged to review the values and principles of Eastern Oregon University . Only complete files of qualified applicants will be reviewed. Eastern Oregon University is an EEO Employer and welcomes applications from women, members of historically underrepresented minority groups, US Veterans, and persons with disabilities. EOU is committed to providing equal opportunity in its recruitment, admissions, educational programs, activities and employment without illegal discrimination on the basis of age, color, disability, national origin, race, marital status, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression or any status as protected by state or federal law. Quick Link to Posting https://eou.peopleadmin.com/postings/3099 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? EOU Website Posting Chronicle of Higher Education State Employment Service DiverseJobs.net Referral by EOU Employee HigherEdJobs.com Newspaper Other If you answered \"Newspaper\" or \"Other\" above, please give specifics here: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Transcripts Portfolio (document1) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Portfolio (document2) Optional Documents Veteran Preference Document To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
