      "title": "University Jobs",
      "description": "University Jobs at EOU | Biology (Human Anatomy &amp; Physiology) Online Adjunct Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help EOU Home HR Home HR Contacts About Union County Biology (Human Anatomy & Physiology) Online Adjunct Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates should submit a letter of interest that addresses relevant expertise, area(s) of teaching interest, qualifications and availability; complete curriculum vitae; and names, addresses and telephone numbers of three professional references, graduate transcripts, a sample syllabi (submit under Portfolio Document 1) and a statement of teaching philosophy. Posting Details Position Information Position Number Position Title Biology (Human Anatomy & Physiology) Online Adjunct Job Description Summary Eastern Oregon University extends its outstanding higher education learning and degree program opportunities nationwide via fully accredited courses using its online learning environment resources. Click here for more detailed information. EOU is soliciting online adjunct applications for qualified online teachers in the following academic discipline: Biology (Human Anatomy and Physiology) – Candidate will teach 200-level Anatomy and Physiology online. Responsibilities Eastern Oregon University invites applications for an adjunct to teach online courses in Anatomy and Physiology in our Biology Program. We seek an energetic, positive professional dedicated to teamwork and high-quality undergraduate instruction with experience in online teaching. The candidate will teach 200-level Anatomy and Physiology. Creates an environment that acknowledges, encourages and celebrates differences. Functions and communicates effectively and respectfully within the context of varying beliefs, behaviors, orientations, identities and cultural backgrounds. Seeks opportunities to gain experience working and collaborating in diverse, multicultural, and inclusive settings with a willingness to change for continual improvement. Adheres to all EOU’s policies including the policies on Prohibited Discrimination & Harassment and the Professional Standards of Conduct. Required Qualifications Graduate Degree in associated discipline Previous experience teaching in post-secondary education Documented capability to learn online learning software application(s) Ability to effectively inspire and teach students from diverse backgrounds and learning styles in online education environment *Successful completion of a EOU background check and submission of valid work authorization documents Preferred Qualifications Terminal Degree in associated discipline One or more years of experience teaching anatomy and physiology in post-secondary, online environment *Competency in the use of an online learning management software application(s) ( i.e. CANVAS , Blackboard, etc.) Posting Detail Information Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Summary Candidates should submit a letter of interest that addresses relevant expertise, area(s) of teaching interest, qualifications and availability; complete curriculum vitae; and names, addresses and telephone numbers of three professional references, graduate transcripts, a sample syllabi (submit under Portfolio Document 1) and a statement of teaching philosophy. Quick Link to Posting https://eou.peopleadmin.com/postings/1824 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? EOU Website Posting Chronicle of Higher Education State Employment Service DiverseJobs.net Referral by EOU Employee HigherEdJobs.com Newspaper Other If you answered \"Newspaper\" or \"Other\" above, please give specifics here: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Transcripts Portfolio (document1) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
