o EOU’s online program); 2) Curriculum vitae with the names, telephone numbers, and email addresses of three professional references; 3) Transcripts (official required for finalists); 4) One-page statement of teaching philosophy. 5) Sample syllabus (use “Portfolio 1” in the online application system to upload the syllabus) 6) Sample of Learning Management System use for online courses (use “Portfolio 2” in the online application system to upload this documentation). Candidates are encouraged to review the values and principles of Eastern Oregon University . Compensation for online adjunct instructors varies by student credit hours and/or student enrollment: * Undergraduate classes enrolling 15 students or less: $47.50 per student credit hour * Undergraduate classes enrolling 16 students or more: $760.00 per credit hour Only complete files of qualified applicants will be reviewed. Applications will be reviewed as they are received, starting October 3, 2025. Quick Link to Posting https://eou.peopleadmin.com/postings/1623 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? EOU Website Posting Chronicle of Higher Education State Employment Service DiverseJobs.net Referral by EOU Employee HigherEdJobs.com Newspaper Other If you answered \"Newspaper\" or \"Other\" above, please give specifics here: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Transcripts Portfolio (document1) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Veteran Preference Document Portfolio (document2) To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
