      "title": "University Jobs",
      "description": "University Jobs at EOU | Literacy Tutor Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help EOU Home HR Home HR Contacts About Union County Literacy Tutor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates are encouraged to review the values and principles of Eastern Oregon University . Only complete files of qualified applicants will be reviewed. Eastern Oregon University – Oregon’s Rural University! – is a respected public, higher education institution of academic excellence. Brilliant faculty and staff thrive and together fulfill their career ambitions to serve students from all walks of life. EOU is a beautiful, quaint campus nestled in a remarkably scenic, high elevation valley populated by wonderful, community-minded citizens that have balanced work-life flexibility. Take a virtual tour of Eastern Oregon University . Special Instructions Eastern Oregon University is an EEO Employer and welcomes applications from women, members of historically underrepresented minority groups, US Veterans, and persons with disabilities. EOU is committed to providing equal opportunity in its recruitment, admissions, educational programs, activities and employment without illegal discrimination on the basis of age, color, disability, national origin, race, marital status, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression or any status as protected by state or federal law. Posting Details Position Information Position Number Position Title Literacy Tutor Job Description Summary Eastern Oregon University Reading Clinic is currently seeking applicants for part-time literacy tutors. Candidates should demonstrate: Ability and willingness to learn specific tutoring techniques and use the provided curricula accurately and effectively. Ability and willingness to learn basic literacy assessment protocols Ability to provide literacy tutoring multiple days per week (3-4) at various times of the day. Ability to work effectively with young children in small groups or one-on-one situations Ability to receive and apply feedback Ability to maintain a positive attitude and a growth mindset while working with children Organizational skills to accurately record student progress daily Ability to communicate effectively with parents and children using both verbal and written communication Responsibilities Plan for and deliver literacy tutoring to young children Administer assessments Record daily student progress Record assessment data Required Qualifications 18 years of age or older. Desire to work with young children Must satisfactorily complete EOU criminal and credential background check. Having a criminal history is not an automatic bar to employment. In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. Eastern Oregon University will not sponsor applicants for employment visas. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with young children Licensed teacher or paraprofessional Previous training in evidence-based literacy methods Posting Detail Information Open Date 06/02/2025 Close Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Summary Candidates are encouraged to review the values and principles of Eastern Oregon University . Only complete files of qualified applicants will be reviewed. Eastern Oregon University – Oregon’s Rural University! – is a respected public, higher education institution of academic excellence. Brilliant faculty and staff thrive and together fulfill their career ambitions to serve students from all walks of life. EOU is a beautiful, quaint campus nestled in a remarkably scenic, high elevation valley populated by wonderful, community-minded citizens that have balanced work-life flexibility. Take a virtual tour of Eastern Oregon University . Special Instructions Eastern Oregon University is an EEO Employer and welcomes applications from women, members of historically underrepresented minority groups, US Veterans, and persons with disabilities. EOU is committed to providing equal opportunity in its recruitment, admissions, educational programs, activities and employment without illegal discrimination on the basis of age, color, disability, national origin, race, marital status, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression or any status as protected by state or federal law. Quick Link to Posting https://eou.peopleadmin.com/postings/3258 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Have you had previous training in teaching reading to children? If so, please describe: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
